# Explicit paths only — never `**`-prefixed globs. Verified 2026-09-24 (Apple
# CLI 1.4.1, one build at a time): a glob set (`**/target/`, `**/.build/`, …)
# transferred 1.07 GB, while the same tree with explicit paths transferred
# 66 MB. After editing, confirm the build logs `transferring context:` in the
# tens of MB.
#
# Apple's CLI reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`, so each app carries
# apps/<app>/Dockerfile.buildkit.dockerignore symlinked here for one source of
# truth. podman/Linux reads this root file directly.

# Version control
.git/

# Rust workspace build output (all apps share the root target/)
target/

# Swift / SwiftPM dependency + artefact cache (~7 GB, 111k files)
apps/yral-ios/packages/YralApp/.build/

# Python virtualenvs (Ansible/Python tooling, not used for image builds)
.venv/
apps/hetzner-bare-metal-fleet/.venv/
apps/yral-rishi-agent/.venv/

# Ansible collections installed into the workspace path by `mise run bootstrap`
ansible/collections/

# Xcode build output
apps/yral-ios/build/